Qa5 9. Bd2 Qa4 10. Ra2 b6 11. Nf3 Ba6 12. Bxa6 Qxa6 13. Qf4 h6 14. g4 Nbc6 15.
Rg1 Rc8 16. Rg3 Ke8 17. Qe3 h5 18. Rh3 Kd7 19. gxh5 Nf5 20. Qd3 Qxd3 21. cxd3
cxd4 22. Rc2 dxc3 23. Rxc3 Ncd4 24. Nxd4 Nxd4 25. Rxc8 Kxc8 26. h6 gxh6 27.
Rxh6 Nf3+ 28. Ke2 Rxh6 29. Bxh6 Nxe5 30. Bg7 Nd7 31. Kf3 Kd8 32. Bc3 Ke7 33.
Kf4 f6 34. Bb4+ Kf7 35. Ke3 Ne5 36. Bd6 Nc6 37. Kd2 b5 38. Kc3 Kg6 39. Kd2 Kf5
40. Ke3 a5 41. Kd2 Kg4 42. Kc3 e5 43. Bc7 a4 44. Bd6 Kh3 45. f4 e4 46. Kd2 f5 {
This game is given in the bulletin as McDonald 0-1 Stisis and that is
consistent with the likely result of the final position BUT the crosstable in
the bulletin (which doesn't include details of colour) gives the result in
favour of McDonald. Note also that McDonald was white in round 7. Perhaps the
strongest argument is that McDonald is a known French defence player whereas I
couldn't find a single French Defence played by Stisis on the database. For
these reasons I am assuming that the colours are given wrongly in the bulletin
and that this game was Stisis 0-1 McDonald (John Saunders, 12 July 2021)} 0-1

